had also finished second, to " [:a {:href "/athletes/72623"} "Naoto Tajima"] ". Those three constituted the Japanese triple jump contingent in Berlin. They would be challenged by Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/64744"} "Jack Metcalfe"] ", who had broken the world record in 1935."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Metcalfe opened with 15.50 (50-10¼), but Tajima took the first round lead with 15.76 (51-8½), and that would be good enough for the gold medal. However, in round four, he broke the sand at 16.00 (52-6) for a world record, 22 centimetres beyond Metcalfe’s mark. Harada moved into second with 15.66 (51-4½) in the final round."] "\n\n" [:p {} "World War II would effectively end Japanese dominance in this event. In " [:a {:href "/results/59030"} "1952"] ", they had a jumper finish 6th, and, in " [:a {:href "/results/59415"} "1956"] ", two of their jumpers placed 7th and 8th, but no Japanese has won a medal in any major international competition since, as of 2024."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "396"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/72623"} "Naoto Tajima"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "– (" [:span {:class "label label-primary"} [:abbrev {:title "No Placement"} "NP"]] ")"] [:td {} "16.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "395"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/72449"} "Masao Harada"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-